def author(c,s,m,a):
 c('b223','旋轉閘門力矩、河潮聯合作用與長期調適~Rotating-gate torque, combined river and tidal effects, and long-term adaptation',['ea-thames','ea-thames40','archives-thames'],r'''
旋轉門體驅動力矩~Rotating-gate drive torque||旋轉閘門的驅動需求來自重量、浮力、水壓與摩擦的合成力矩。各力臂隨角度改變，最大水壓不一定對應最大驅動需求。~Drive demand combines moments from weight, buoyancy, water pressure and friction. Lever arms vary with angle, so maximum water pressure need not coincide with maximum required drive torque.||假設某角度水壓合力4 MN、力臂1.5 m，重量與浮力淨力矩−2 MN·m，摩擦0.5 MN·m；需求4.5 MN·m，僅該姿態靜力。~At one assumed angle, water force 4 MN acts at 1.5 m, net weight-buoyancy moment is −2 MN·m and friction is 0.5 MN·m. Required torque is 4.5 MN·m for that static posture only.||沿轉角建立分項力矩曲線，對照油壓、位置與轉速資料；分開啟動摩擦和持續轉動阻力，避免只用終點水位解釋整段動作。~Build component moment curves against angle and compare pressure, position and speed. Separate breakaway friction from running resistance instead of explaining an entire movement by the final water level.||密封摩擦、沉積物與軸承偏心會讓負載峰值偏離理想曲線。若只以平均馬達功率檢查能力，短暫的起動高扭矩和局部拘束可能被完全掩蓋。~Seal friction, sediment and bearing eccentricity shift peaks away from ideal curves. Average motor power can conceal brief breakaway torque demands and local restraint that govern actual motion capability.||最大水壓時刻不一定就是最大驅動力矩時刻。~Maximum water pressure need not coincide with maximum drive torque.
暴潮相位與潮汐疊加~Surge phase and tidal superposition||天文潮與氣象暴潮的峰值可能不同時到達。簡單線性相加可說明相位重要性，真實河口中摩擦與水深又使交互作用非線性。~Astronomical tide and meteorological surge can peak at different times. Linear addition illustrates phase effects, while friction and changing depth make real estuarine interaction nonlinear.||假設潮位2cosθ m、暴潮1cos(θ+60°) m，合成振幅√(2²+1²+2×2×1cos60°)=2.646 m，非兩峰直接相加3 m。~Assume tide 2cosθ m and surge 1cos(θ+60°) m. Combined amplitude is √(2²+1²+2×2×1cos60°)=2.646 m, rather than the direct peak sum of 3 m.||把不同來源水位換到同一時間與高程基準，檢查預報相位誤差；比較水深不同期間的殘差，以辨識線性疊加何時不再適用。~Convert water levels to common time and elevation references and examine phase errors. Compare residuals across different depths to identify when linear superposition ceases to represent the estuary.||取兩個不同時刻的最大值相加可能過度保守，也可能忽略風暴改變潮波傳播後的新峰值。模型驗證若只比最高水位，會漏掉危險持續時間。~Adding maxima from separate times can be overly conservative yet still miss peaks created by changed tidal propagation. Validation limited to peak level overlooks the duration of hazardous conditions.||兩個峰值的算術和不一定是實際聯合峰值。~The arithmetic sum of two peaks need not be the combined peak.
關閉期間河水蓄積~River storage during closure||阻隔海潮時，上游河流仍持續入流，受保護河段因此變成暫時蓄水體。可用庫容取決於沿岸高程與支流，不能只看閘前水位。~When sea levels are excluded, river inflow continues and the protected reach temporarily stores water. Available storage depends on bank elevations and tributaries, not only the level beside the barrier.||假設關閉期間淨入流300 m³/s持續2 h、有效水面20 km²，Δh=Qt/A=0.108 m；忽略側向溢流與面積隨水位變化。~Assume net inflow 300 m³/s for two hours over effective area 20 km². Δh=Qt/A=0.108 m, excluding lateral spill and changes of area with stage.||用上游流量、支流雨量與多站水位建立同期水量平衡，檢查水面坡度是否仍可用單一儲水面積描述；另計未量測的側向流入。~Build a synchronized balance from river flow, tributary rainfall and multiple water-level stations. Test whether one storage area still represents the water-surface slope and estimate unmeasured lateral inflow separately.||只防海側高水位而忽略河流洪峰，可能把洪水留在防線內側。以平坦水面替代長河段水力坡降，還會低估某些支流交會處的局部水位。~Excluding the sea while overlooking a river flood can retain water inside the defence. Replacing a long river gradient with a flat surface can underestimate levels near particular tributary junctions.||關閘排除海水後，上游水位仍可能持續上升。~Upstream water can continue rising after the sea is excluded.
通航窗口與排程~Navigation windows and scheduling||活動防洪結構同時是航運通道，通航窗口受水位、橋下空間與設備可用性約束。平均船舶到達率無法描述尖峰排隊與關閉後的復原時間。~A movable flood defence is also a navigation route. Windows depend on level, clearance and availability; average vessel arrivals do not describe peak queues or recovery after a closure.||假設停航3 h、到達率4 vessels/h，累積12 vessels；重開後處理6 vessels/h且仍到達4 vessels/h，清空需12/(6−4)=6 h。~Assume closure three hours with arrival rate four vessels per hour, accumulating twelve vessels. After reopening, service six and arrivals four per hour require 12/(6−4)=6 hours to clear.||用匿名化船舶到達與通過時間畫累積曲線，核對服務率是否受船型和潮向影響；將安全間隔和商業需求分列，避免把理論容量當保證。~Plot cumulative anonymous arrival and transit records, checking vessel-type and tidal effects on service rate. Separate safety spacing from commercial demand instead of presenting theoretical capacity as guaranteed throughput.||若重開後服務率只等於到達率，既有隊列永遠無法消散。把通過閘區的時間與完整航段時間混用，則會錯算容量並掩蓋航道瓶頸。~If reopened service merely matches arrivals, the existing queue never clears. Mixing barrier-crossing time with complete-route time miscalculates capacity and conceals bottlenecks elsewhere in the navigation channel.||重開通道不代表等待隊列會立即消失。~Reopening a route does not immediately eliminate its waiting queue.
門槽沉積與淨空~Gate-recess sediment and clearance||下沉式門體需要特定運動空間，門槽沉積改變淨空與局部水流。平均淤積厚度不能代表單個硬物或高點，幾何檢查必須覆蓋整段掃掠體積。~A recessed gate requires a defined swept space. Sediment changes clearance and local flow, while average deposit thickness cannot represent isolated hard objects or high spots across that volume.||假設槽底面積400 m²、均勻淤積厚0.08 m，沉積體積32 m³；若濕容重16 kN/m³，重量512 kN，不代表驅動附加力。~Assume recess area 400 m² with uniform deposit 0.08 m thick: volume 32 m³. At wet unit weight 16 kN/m³, weight is 512 kN, not the added drive force.||用可重複定位的測深與影像核對槽底高點，區分鬆散泥砂和硬質異物；把門體掃掠幾何疊合測量面，保存清理前後差異。~Use repeatable bathymetry and imagery to identify high spots and distinguish loose sediment from hard debris. Overlay the gate swept volume on surveyed surfaces and preserve before-and-after changes.||均勻沉積假設會低估孤立塊體造成的卡阻，移除沉積也可能暴露既有底板損傷。若只用挖除體積驗收，不能證明全部運動空間已恢復。~Uniform deposits underestimate jamming from isolated blocks, and removal can expose existing sill damage. Excavated volume alone cannot establish that the entire required swept space has been restored.||清出的泥砂總量不能證明所有門槽淨空足夠。~Removed sediment volume does not prove adequate clearance everywhere.
液壓功率與效率~Hydraulic power and efficiency||液壓驅動把流體壓力與流量轉成機械功率，泵的電功率還包含損失。相同壓力下流量不足會降低速度，不能只憑壓力表判斷動作能力。~Hydraulic drives convert pressure and flow into mechanical power, while electrical input also covers losses. Insufficient flow reduces speed even at normal pressure, so a gauge alone cannot establish movement capability.||假設壓差12 MPa、流量0.02 m³/s、總效率0.8，輸入功率ΔpQ/η=300 kW；穩定流量，未含加速與儲能器瞬態。~Assume pressure difference 12 MPa, flow 0.02 m³/s and overall efficiency 0.8. Input ΔpQ/η=300 kW, for steady flow without acceleration or accumulator transients.||同步量測油壓、流量、溫度和門位速率，比較液壓輸入與機械輸出；確認量測位置是在泵側或缸側，避免把管路損失重複計入。~Measure pressure, flow, temperature and gate speed together, comparing hydraulic input with mechanical output. Identify pump-side versus cylinder-side measurements to avoid double-counting line losses.||內漏使壓力維持但有效行程流量減少，油溫上升又改變黏度。只檢查電流或單點壓力，可能把效率惡化誤認為正常的負載變動。~Internal leakage can preserve pressure while reducing useful cylinder flow, and heating changes viscosity. Current or pressure alone may make declining efficiency look like an ordinary change in external loading.||正常油壓不代表有足夠流量完成預定動作。~Normal hydraulic pressure does not guarantee sufficient useful flow.
防線接續高程~Continuous defence elevations||防洪閘與兩岸堤牆必須形成連續高程線，局部低點會繞過強大的主結構。水位基準、沉降與門檻高程的差異往往比平均牆高更重要。~Barrier and bank defences must form a continuous elevation line. Local low points bypass strong main structures, making datum consistency, settlement and sill elevation more important than average wall height.||假設牆頂高程5.8 m、評估水位5.1 m、沉降0.12 m，剩餘幾何超高0.58 m；不含波浪上衝或統計安全裕度。~Assume crest elevation 5.8 m, assessed water level 5.1 m and settlement 0.12 m. Remaining geometric freeboard is 0.58 m, excluding wave runup and probabilistic margins.||沿整條防線進行共同基準閉合水準測量，標出接頭、道路與管線穿越低點；將最新沉降速率與地圖版本一起保存，避免混用不同年代高程。~Run closed leveling on a common datum along the full defence, marking joints, roads and utility crossings. Retain settlement rates and map versions to prevent mixing elevations from different surveys.||主閘設計再強也不能彌補遠端牆頂低點，局部沉降又可能持續發展。以地圖等高線代替接縫精密測量，會把繞流通道藏在資料解析度之下。~A strong main barrier cannot compensate for a distant low crest, and settlement may continue. Coarse map contours can hide bypass routes that require detailed joint and crossing surveys.||主閘足夠高不代表整條沿岸防線都足夠高。~An adequate main barrier does not establish continuous shoreline protection.
波浪脈衝與反力~Wave impulse and reaction||波浪撞擊的峰值和持續時間共同決定脈衝，短脈衝對柔性構件的作用不同於同峰值的長載重。靜水壓力不能替代瞬態結構反應。~Wave impact depends on both peak and duration. A short impulse affects a flexible member differently from a sustained load of equal peak, so hydrostatics cannot substitute for transient structural response.||假設三角形力脈衝峰值2 MN、歷時0.4 s，衝量J=FmaxΔt/2=0.4 MN·s；未由此直接求位移或疲勞。~Assume a triangular force pulse with peak 2 MN and duration 0.4 s. Impulse J=FmaxΔt/2=0.4 MN·s; displacement and fatigue are not obtained from this alone.||用足夠取樣率的壓力和加速度訊號核對脈衝形狀，查濾波是否削掉短峰；再比較脈衝歷時與結構自振週期，決定動力模型層級。~Check pulse shape with sufficiently sampled pressure and acceleration records, examining whether filtering removes brief peaks. Compare duration with structural natural period to choose an appropriate dynamic model.||低取樣率可能完全漏掉撞擊峰值，過度放大峰值而忽略面積與相位也會誤判總力。氣泡含量及局部接觸使相鄰壓力計不一定同步到峰。~Low sampling may miss impact peaks, while multiplying one peak over the entire area misstates total force. Air content and local contact mean adjacent sensors need not peak simultaneously.||局部瞬時壓力峰值不能直接代表整門瞬時合力。~One local pressure peak does not represent the whole-gate resultant.
檢測覆蓋與可用度~Test coverage and availability||定期測試只能發現被測功能的故障，無法保證未施加的環境與荷載。檢測間隔與潛伏失效機率相關，但獨立恆定失效率只是基礎模型。~Periodic tests reveal only exercised failures, not untested environments and loads. Test interval influences latent unavailability, but constant independent failure rate is only a basic model.||假設潛伏失效率λ=0.0002/day、完全檢測間隔30 days，平均不可用度近似λT/2=0.003；限λT很小及完美檢測。~Assume latent failure rate λ=0.0002/day and perfect-test interval 30 days. Mean unavailability is approximately λT/2=0.003, for small λT and complete detection.||列出每項演練涵蓋的感測、傳動與負載條件，將未涵蓋功能保留在分析中；把檢出時間、修復時間和停機原因分別記錄。~List sensors, transmission paths and loading conditions covered by each exercise, retaining uncovered functions in the assessment. Record discovery time, repair time and outage cause separately.||若測試只能檢出部分故障，延續使用完美檢測公式會低估風險。維修造成的暫時停用也屬可用度問題，不能因主設備故障率低就忽略。~Using perfect-test formulas when only some failures are detectable understates risk. Maintenance outages also reduce availability and cannot be ignored merely because the main equipment has a low failure rate.||一次測試成功不等於所有失效模式都已受測。~One successful test does not cover every possible failure mode.
海平面情境與調適~Sea-level scenarios and adaptation||長期海平面變化會改變關閉頻率、河流排水窗口和維護時間，而不只提高一道設計水位。情境外推用來比較方案，並非保證未來趨勢。~Long-term sea-level change affects closure frequency, drainage windows and maintenance time, not only a design level. Scenario extrapolation compares options rather than guaranteeing a future trend.||假設線性相對海平面上升5 mm/year持續40 years，增量0.20 m；另假設加速項0.05 mm/year²，額外0.5at²=0.04 m。~Assume linear relative sea-level rise 5 mm/year over 40 years, giving 0.20 m. An assumed acceleration 0.05 mm/year² adds 0.5at²=0.04 m.||把潮位站、地面沉降與情境模型的基準年份對齊，分列觀測趨勢和規劃假設；比較超高、排水時間及設備使用次數對不同情境的敏感性。~Align baseline years for tide gauges, land movement and scenarios. Separate observed trends from planning assumptions and compare freeboard, drainage duration and equipment-cycle sensitivity across scenarios.||以單一線性速率規劃全部壽命，可能忽略加速、區域沉降與潮汐改變。若只加高牆體而不評估關閉增加，設備疲勞和內河排水需求仍可能失配。~One linear rate may miss acceleration, local subsidence and tidal change. Raising walls without examining more frequent closures can leave equipment fatigue and inland drainage demands poorly matched.||長期調適不能只把預估海平面增量加到牆頂。~Long-term adaptation is more than adding projected rise to crest height.
''')
 for i,ex,out,un in [(1,'4*1.5-2+.5',4.5,'MN m'),(2,'math.sqrt(4+1+4*math.cos(math.pi/3))',2.64575131,'m'),(3,'300*7200/20e6',.108,'m'),(4,'3*4/(6-4)',6,'h'),(5,'400*.08*16',512,'kN'),(6,'12e6*.02/.8/1000',300,'kW'),(7,'5.8-5.1-.12',.58,'m'),(8,'2*.4/2',.4,'MN s'),(9,'.0002*30/2',.003,'probability'),(10,'.5*.05*40**2/1000',.04,'m')]:a('b223',i,ex,out,un)
 c('b224','浮動翻板、壓縮空氣與潟湖環境的耦合~Coupling buoyant flap gates, compressed air and lagoon environmental response',['mose-test','venice-first','abb-mose'],r'''
浮力翻轉與重心~Buoyant rotation and centroids||翻板內水被空氣置換後，浮力和自重對鉸軸的力矩改變，門體才會轉動。上浮不是氣壓直接把整片門推出水面，還必須考慮外部水壓和重心位置。~Replacing internal water with air changes buoyancy and weight moments about the hinge. Rotation is not simply air pressure pushing the entire gate upward; external pressure and centroid positions also matter.||取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設有效排水體積500 m³、海水密度1025 kg/m³、浮力臂3 m，自重3 MN、重心臂4 m；淨復原矩為3.083 MN·m，限靜水姿態。~Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume displaced volume 500 m³, seawater density 1025 kg/m³, buoyancy arm 3 m, weight 3 MN and weight arm 4 m. Net restoring moment is 3.083 MN·m for that hydrostatic posture.||以門角、內外水位與艙氣壓同步重建排水體積，將浮心與重心分開定位；檢查力矩符號是否隨角度改變，避免只比較總浮力與重量。~Reconstruct displacement from synchronized angle, internal and external levels and air pressure. Locate buoyancy and gravity centroids separately and check moment signs as angle changes instead of comparing forces alone.||氣室進水不均會移動重心，改變各鉸座受力。若把完全浸沒的浮力公式沿用到出水後，排水體積與力臂都會錯，進而誤判平衡角度。~Unequal flooding shifts the center of gravity and hinge reactions. Reusing fully submerged buoyancy after emergence gives incorrect displacement and lever arms, leading to a false equilibrium angle.||總浮力大於自重仍不足以決定翻板的平衡角。~Buoyancy exceeding weight does not determine a flap equilibrium angle.
氣壓水深與絕對壓力~Air pressure and absolute pressure||排水用空氣必須克服水深造成的外壓，壓縮氣體的狀態方程則使用絕對壓力。把表壓帶入氣體體積換算，會造成系統性的質量估算錯誤。~Displacement air must overcome external water pressure, while gas state relations require absolute pressure. Inserting gauge pressure into volume conversion systematically miscalculates air mass.||取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設海水深8 m、密度1025 kg/m³、大氣壓101.3 kPa，靜水表壓80.442 kPa、絕壓181.742 kPa；不含管損與動態壓差。~Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume seawater depth 8 m, density 1025 kg/m³ and atmospheric pressure 101.3 kPa. Gauge pressure is 80.442 kPa and absolute pressure 181.742 kPa, excluding piping losses and dynamics.||標明每支壓力計為表壓或絕壓，核對取壓點高程和當時大氣壓；利用獨立水位量測交叉檢查氣壓所推得的水柱高度。~Identify each gauge as relative or absolute, checking tapping elevation and atmospheric pressure. Cross-check the water-column height inferred from air pressure against independent level measurements.||導壓管積水會改變零點，溫度變動也會使封閉氣體壓力改變。若只用壓力上升判斷門位，可能把管路堵塞或熱效應當成正常浮升。~Water in impulse lines changes zero, and temperature changes pressure in confined air. Pressure rise alone can therefore mistake blockage or thermal effects for the expected gate movement.||氣體狀態換算不能把表壓當成絕對壓力。~Gas-state calculations cannot substitute gauge pressure for absolute pressure.
空氣供應與壓縮功~Air supply and compression work||壓縮機功率取決於壓比、流量、熱交換和效率，注入體積不是同壓力下的自由空氣體積。理想等溫模型提供能耗下界，不能代表真實機組效率。~Compressor power depends on pressure ratio, flow, heat exchange and efficiency. Delivered volume is not free-air volume at the same pressure. Ideal isothermal work is a lower-bound model, not an actual machine rating.||假設自由空氣流量2 m³/s、入口絕壓100 kPa、出口200 kPa，等溫理想功率p1Q1ln(p2/p1)=138.63 kW；未含機械與熱損失。~Assume free-air flow 2 m³/s, inlet absolute pressure 100 kPa and outlet 200 kPa. Ideal isothermal power p1Q1ln(p2/p1)=138.63 kW, excluding mechanical and thermal losses.||記錄流量換算的參考溫壓，對照壓縮機入口出口狀態和電功率；用儲氣壓力變化核對總氣量平衡，避免把瞬時充氣量當長期平均。~Record flow reference temperature and pressure, comparing compressor inlet and outlet states with electrical power. Cross-check air balance using storage-pressure change rather than treating transient filling as a steady average.||壓縮熱若未散去，等溫假設會低估功率；漏氣又使供氣量不等於有效排水量。把氣量和門體位移直接一對一換算，會漏掉可壓縮儲能。~Incomplete heat rejection makes the isothermal estimate optimistic, and leakage separates supplied air from effective displacement. Equating air volume directly with gate movement ignores compressible energy stored in the system.||供氣量增加不一定等比例增加翻板排水體積。~More supplied air need not proportionally increase displaced water volume.
鉸座荷載分配~Hinge reaction distribution||多鉸座承受門體合力時，構件剛度與安裝高差控制分配，均分只適用對稱理想情況。局部接觸與變形會讓一個鉸座先承載。~When several hinges share a gate resultant, stiffness and installation offsets govern distribution. Equal sharing is an ideal symmetric case; local contact and deformation may load one support first.||假設兩鉸座間距8 m、合力6 MN偏心1 m，靜力反力R1=3+6/8=3.75 MN、R2=2.25 MN；限剛性門體與平面荷載。~Assume hinge spacing 8 m and resultant 6 MN offset 1 m. Reactions are R1=3+6/8=3.75 MN and R2=2.25 MN, for a rigid gate under planar loading.||把鉸座幾何、軸承間隙和應變訊號一起核對，確認反力和等於外載且力矩平衡；不同門角分別作圖，找出接觸改變的轉折。~Compare hinge geometry, bearing clearance and strain, checking that reactions sum to applied load and balance its moment. Plot separate gate angles to identify changes in contact.||把兩鉸座固定均分會低估偏心側承載，腐蝕或間隙改變又可能造成重新分配。只有總合力監測，無法辨識單個連接件的局部超載。~Fixed equal sharing underestimates the eccentric side, while corrosion and clearance changes redistribute load. Monitoring total resultant alone cannot identify overload in one individual connection or bearing.||兩座鉸鏈存在不代表各自永遠承受一半荷載。~Two hinges do not necessarily carry half the load each.
波浪激振與自振~Wave excitation and natural period||浮動門體具有轉動慣性、復原剛度與水體附加慣性，波浪頻率接近自振時可能放大運動。乾態模態不能直接替代濕態動力特性。~A buoyant gate has rotational inertia, restoring stiffness and added hydrodynamic inertia. Excitation near its natural frequency can amplify motion, so dry structural modes cannot replace wet dynamic properties.||假設含附加水慣性的I=8×10⁸ kg·m²、線性轉動剛度K=2×10⁸ N·m/rad，T=2π√(I/K)=12.566 s；限小擾動。~Assume inertia including added water I=8×10⁸ kg·m² and linear rotational stiffness K=2×10⁸ N·m/rad. T=2π√(I/K)=12.566 s, for small disturbances.||比較門角和波面頻譜，辨認相位及阻尼而非只找相同頻率；在不同水深重估附加慣性，確認觀測峰值不是感測器安裝共振。~Compare angle and wave spectra, examining phase and damping rather than frequency coincidence alone. Reassess added inertia at different depths and rule out resonance of sensor mountings.||大角度運動會改變浮力剛度，破壞線性週期假設；相鄰門片的流體耦合也會產生集體模態。以單片門的小振幅結果代表整列，可能漏掉相對運動。~Large angles alter restoring stiffness and invalidate a linear period. Hydrodynamic coupling produces collective modes, so a single-gate small-motion result can miss relative movement across the full barrier.||乾態自振週期不能直接代表水中浮門的週期。~A dry natural period does not directly describe a submerged buoyant gate.
相鄰門片相對位移~Relative motion between gates||兩片門同方向移動時，相對間隙可能很小；反相時則可能最大。接觸風險取決於相對運動與公差，不能只看每片門的最大位移。~Two gates moving together can have small relative displacement, while opposing phases can maximize it. Contact risk depends on relative motion and tolerances, not each gate maximum independently.||假設兩門邊緣振幅各0.04 m、相位差120°，相對振幅√(A1²+A2²−2A1A2cosφ)=0.06928 m；同頻正弦近似。~Assume edge amplitudes 0.04 m each and phase difference 120°. Relative amplitude √(A1²+A2²−2A1A2cosφ)=0.06928 m, for equal-frequency sinusoidal motion.||同步量測相鄰門角並換算同一高度的邊緣位移，保留相位資訊；把靜態公差、熱變形與動態間隙分列，檢查時間同步誤差。~Synchronize adjacent gate angles and convert them to edge displacement at one elevation. Retain phase and separate static tolerance, thermal distortion and dynamic clearance, checking synchronization error.||兩套感測器若時鐘不一致，可能製造假的反相訊號。反之只存最大振幅會丟失相位，無法判定是否同時接近，造成不必要或不足的碰撞評估。~Unsynchronized clocks can create a false out-of-phase response. Saving only maximum amplitudes loses phase, preventing determination of simultaneous approach and producing either excessive or insufficient collision assessment.||兩片門振幅相同仍可能具有很大的相對運動。~Equal individual amplitudes can still produce substantial relative motion.
關閉潟湖降雨收支~Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon||防潮時海口交換減少，但潟湖降雨和陸域排水仍在加入水量。水面面積使水位對體積敏感度不同，內部風致增水又會打破均勻水位假設。~Reducing inlet exchange does not stop rainfall or land drainage into the lagoon. Surface area controls stage sensitivity to volume, while wind setup can invalidate a uniform water level assumption.||假設封閉水面100 km²、降雨20 mm且全部直接入水，增量2 million m³、水位上升0.02 m；未含陸域逕流、蒸發或漏流。~Assume isolated surface area 100 km² and direct rainfall 20 mm. Added volume is 2 million m³ and mean rise 0.02 m, excluding land runoff, evaporation and leakage.||對照雨量雷達、雨量站和內外潮位，建立分時水量平衡；用不同方位水位站辨識風致傾斜，避免把單站升高全歸因於降雨。~Compare radar, rain gauges and internal and external levels in a time-resolved balance. Use stations on different shores to identify wind setup instead of attributing all local rise to rainfall.||將整個流域雨量直接乘潟湖面積會混淆陸地與水面貢獻，地下水和支流也有延遲。只看封閉後平均水位，可能漏掉城市沿岸的局部高水位。~Multiplying catchment rain by lagoon area confuses land and open-water contributions, while groundwater and tributaries are delayed. Mean lagoon level can miss locally higher levels along urban shores.||海口關閉並不代表潟湖內的水量保持不變。~Closing inlets does not keep lagoon water volume constant.
鹽分混合與交換~Salinity mixing and exchange||鹽分守恆可追蹤海水與淡水比例，但潟湖並非瞬間完全混合。底層密度流和局部滯水會讓平均鹽度掩蓋生態差異。~Salt conservation tracks seawater and freshwater fractions, but a lagoon does not mix instantly. Bottom density currents and stagnant regions allow a mean salinity to conceal ecological variation.||假設初始100 million m³水體鹽度30 g/kg，加入5 million m³淡水，同密度完全混合；新鹽度30×100/105=28.571 g/kg，無蒸發。~Assume 100 million m³ at 30 g/kg plus 5 million m³ freshwater, equal densities and complete mixing. New salinity is 30×100/105=28.571 g/kg, without evaporation.||採集表中底層鹽溫剖面，核對混合前後水量與導電度校正；對照潮相與支流入流，判斷單一平均值是否足以描述鹽分分布。~Sample surface, middle and bottom salinity-temperature profiles and verify volume balance and conductivity calibration. Compare tides and tributary inputs to test whether one average adequately describes the distribution.||底層高鹽水可在表面變淡時仍滯留，造成密度分層並限制氧氣交換。把所有鹽度變化都歸因於門片動作，會漏掉河流、風和蒸發影響。~Saline bottom water can remain after surface freshening, maintaining stratification and limiting oxygen exchange. Attributing every salinity change to gate movement overlooks river, wind and evaporation effects.||平均鹽度下降不代表底層高鹽水已完全排出。~Lower mean salinity does not prove complete removal of saline bottom water.
壓力量測與不確定度~Pressure measurement uncertainty||以壓力反推水深時，密度與感測誤差都進入結果。壓力計精度不是整體水位精度，導壓高程、氣泡和溫度也需要校核。~Inferring depth from pressure involves both density and sensor error. Transducer accuracy is not complete level accuracy because tapping elevation, trapped air and temperature also require checking.||取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設壓力標準不確定度500 Pa、密度1025 kg/m³且暫視為精確，uh=up/(ρg)=0.04973 m；僅此誤差分量，非總誤差。~Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume pressure standard uncertainty 500 Pa and density 1025 kg/m³ treated as exact. uh=up/(ρg)=0.04973 m, representing this component only rather than total error.||以可追溯壓力基準校正量測鏈，檢查零點和跨度，再與獨立水位及溫鹽資料比較；把隨機不確定度和共同基準偏差分開列帳。~Calibrate the measurement chain with a traceable pressure reference, checking zero and span. Compare independent level and temperature-salinity data, separating random uncertainty from common datum bias.||共同導壓管堵塞會讓多支感測器一致但錯誤，不能用數字吻合當獨立證據。若海水密度變動仍沿用淡水換算，也會產生持續水深偏差。~A shared blocked impulse line can make several sensors agree incorrectly. Agreement is not independence, and using freshwater density for changing seawater creates a persistent inferred-depth bias.||壓力感測器一致不代表其共同取壓條件正確。~Sensor agreement does not prove their shared pressure connection is correct.
供氣網路可用度~Air-network availability||供氣系統由壓縮、儲存、分配與閥件共同構成，備援壓縮機無法補償所有共用管路故障。可靠度必須先定義功能成功條件再計算。~Air supply comprises compression, storage, distribution and valves. A spare compressor cannot compensate for every shared-pipe fault, so reliability calculations require a defined functional success condition.||假設兩台獨立壓縮機可用度各0.98、任一足夠，並串聯共同分配系統0.99；A=(1−0.02²)×0.99=0.989604，忽略修復動態。~Assume two independent compressors each available 0.98, either sufficient, in series with distribution availability 0.99. A=(1−0.02²)×0.99=0.989604, excluding repair dynamics.||從供氣需求追蹤至末端閥件，標出共用電源和管段，核對備機是否真能滿足所需流量；用歷史故障分類檢查獨立性假設。~Trace supply demand to terminal valves, marking common power and pipe sections. Verify that a spare truly provides required flow and use historical failure categories to test independence assumptions.||共用閥卡住或管道淹水會使兩台壓縮機同時無法供氣，即使各自運轉正常。將設備啟動成功當作末端功能成功，會高估整體可用度。~A stuck shared valve or flooded pipe can defeat both running compressors. Equating successful equipment start with successful terminal delivery overstates availability of the complete functional supply chain.||備機能啟動不代表末端一定取得足夠供氣。~A starting standby machine does not guarantee adequate terminal air delivery.
''')
 for i,ex,out,un in [(1,'1025*9.81*500*3/1e6-3*4',3.082875,'MN m'),(2,'101.3+1025*9.81*8/1000',181.742,'kPa absolute'),(3,'100*2*math.log(2)',138.629436,'kW'),(4,'3+6/8',3.75,'MN'),(5,'2*math.pi*math.sqrt(8e8/2e8)',12.5663706,'s'),(6,'math.sqrt(2*.04**2-2*.04**2*math.cos(2*math.pi/3))',.06928203,'m'),(7,'100e6*.02',2e6,'m3'),(8,'30*100/105',28.5714286,'g/kg'),(9,'500/(1025*9.81)',.04972527,'m'),(10,'(1-.02**2)*.99',.989604,'availability')]:a('b224',i,ex,out,un)
 c('b225','都市逕流、潮位排水、抽水能源與水庫水質~Urban runoff, tidal drainage, pumping energy and reservoir water quality',['pub-marina','pub-marina-faq','pub-marina-book'],r'''
集水區逕流峰值~Catchment runoff peak||都市不透水面提高快速逕流比例，但降雨空間與集流時間控制峰值。合理化公式適合指定的小型集水區條件，不能直接代表整個大型水庫入流歷線。~Impervious surfaces increase rapid runoff, while rainfall distribution and concentration time control the peak. The rational method applies to specified small-catchment conditions, not a complete large-reservoir inflow hydrograph.||假設集水區2 km²、C=0.75、雨強60 mm/h且歷時超過集流時間；Q=0.278CiA=25.02 m³/s，未含渠道滯蓄。~Assume area 2 km², C=0.75 and intensity 60 mm/h lasting beyond concentration time. Q=0.278CiA=25.02 m³/s, excluding channel storage.||用雨量站與雷達核對雨強是否覆蓋集水區，再比較出口流量和延遲；將土地利用變更、排水分區和所選集流時間附在計算表。~Check rain-gauge and radar coverage, then compare outlet flow and lag. Attach land-use changes, drainage boundaries and chosen concentration time to the calculation record.||短時局部暴雨可能不符合均勻降雨假設，排水瓶頸也會改變峰值時間。把每個分區峰值直接相加，可能錯估各峰不同時到達的真實入流。~Brief localized storms violate uniform rainfall assumptions, and drainage bottlenecks alter peak timing. Adding every subcatchment peak directly can misrepresent the actual combined inflow when peaks arrive at different times.||各分區最大流量不能在沒有時序資料下直接相加。~Subcatchment peaks cannot simply be added without their timing.
庫容與淨入流~Storage and net inflow||水庫水位變化由入流減去閘排、抽水及其他出流決定。庫面不是永遠固定，低窪岸帶開始淹沒時，水位與庫容的關係會改變。~Reservoir level changes with inflow minus gravity discharge, pumping and other losses. Surface area is not always constant; inundating low banks changes the stage-storage relation.||假設淨入流80 m³/s持續30 min、有效水面3 km²，Δh=Qt/A=0.048 m；只作固定面積短時估算。~Assume net inflow 80 m³/s over thirty minutes and effective area 3 km². Δh=Qt/A=0.048 m, a short-duration constant-area estimate.||將每個流量來源按相同時間步積分，對照實測庫容變化；檢查水位站是否受局部風浪或排水噴流影響，再辨認水量平衡殘差。~Integrate each flow source on identical time steps and compare measured storage change. Check gauges for local waves or discharge jets before interpreting the water-balance residual.||抽水流量若採額定值而非當時揚程下的實際值，會產生虛假的未量測入流。時間步太長又可能把短時高峰平滑掉，低估岸邊淹水機會。~Using rated pump discharge instead of flow at actual head creates false unexplained inflow. Long time steps smooth brief peaks and can underestimate opportunities for flooding along the reservoir edge.||水位不變不代表沒有大量水量流入與流出。~An unchanged level does not imply negligible inflow and outflow.
低潮重力排水~Low-tide gravity drainage||庫水高於海水時可由水頭差驅動排水，潮位反轉則可能失去這項能力。閘口流況隨上下游淹沒程度改變，單一係數不能代表全部潮相。~A positive reservoir-to-sea head can drive gravity drainage, but tidal reversal removes it. Opening hydraulics vary with downstream submergence, so one coefficient does not describe every tide.||取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設有效孔口20 m²、Cd=0.65、水頭差0.5 m；Q=CdA√(2gΔh)=40.72 m³/s，限淹沒孔口準穩定流。~Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume effective opening 20 m², Cd=0.65 and head difference 0.5 m. Q=CdA√(2gΔh)=40.72 m³/s, for quasi-steady submerged-orifice flow.||同步核對內外水位、開口面積及流向，將資料分成淹沒與自由出流型態；以實測流量校正係數，並保留潮位快速變化期間的偏差。~Synchronize internal and external levels, opening area and flow direction. Separate submerged and free-outflow regimes, calibrate coefficients with measured discharge and retain rapid-tide residuals.||水頭接近零時儀器偏差可能比真實差值更大，造成錯判流向。忽略海側波浪與回流時，即使平均水頭為正，也不能保證瞬間全向外排水。~Near zero head, instrument bias may exceed the real difference and reverse the inferred direction. Waves and return currents can create inward flow even with positive mean outward head.||平均庫位較高不保證所有瞬間都向海排水。~A higher mean reservoir level does not ensure outward flow at every instant.
高平均潮位抽水~Pumping against elevated tide||抽水把水量提升到較高海側水位，需要克服靜揚程和管路損失。功率隨流量與揚程變化，不能用固定每立方公尺能耗描述所有潮況。~Pumping lifts water against sea level and conveyance losses. Power varies with both flow and head, so a fixed energy per cubic metre cannot describe all tidal conditions.||取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。假設淡水Q=20 m³/s、總揚程3 m、總效率0.8；輸入P=ρgQH/η=735.75 kW，不含啟動電流或備援負載。~Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Assume fresh-water flow 20 m³/s, total head 3 m and overall efficiency 0.8. Input P=ρgQH/η=735.75 kW, excluding starting current and auxiliary backup loads.||核對泵前後壓力、流量與電表，分列靜揚程和沿程損失；把效率對應到實際工況，不能以最佳效率點替代高海潮期間的效率。~Compare suction and delivery pressure, flow and metered electricity. Separate static head from line loss and use efficiency at the actual operating point rather than the best-efficiency value during high tide.||揚程增加可能使泵流量下降，同時改變效率與振動。只看設備已通電會高估排水能力；忽略輔助設備能耗也會低估整場暴雨的能源需求。~Increasing head may reduce pump flow while changing efficiency and vibration. Energized equipment does not establish drainage capacity, and omitting auxiliary loads understates energy required for the complete storm event.||抽水機正在運轉不等於達到額定排水流量。~A running pump does not necessarily deliver its rated flow.
並聯泵與系統曲線~Parallel pumps and system curve||並聯泵共享同一出水系統，增加機組會提高管損，單機工作點也移動。因此兩台流量不是把單台自由出水流量直接相加。~Parallel pumps share a discharge system. Adding units increases losses and shifts each operating point, so combined flow is not simply twice a single pump free-discharge rate.||曲線採H以m、q與Q以m³/s表示；截距10、2的單位為m，係數0.01、0.005的單位均為s²/m⁵。假設單泵H=10−0.01q²、系統H=2+0.005Q²，兩泵相同且Q=2q；解得Q=√(8/0.0075)=32.66 m³/s。~For these dimensional curves H is in m and q and Q are in m³/s. Intercepts 10 and 2 have units m; coefficients 0.01 and 0.005 both have units s²/m⁵. Assume each pump H=10−0.01q² and system H=2+0.005Q², with two identical pumps Q=2q. Solving gives Q=√(8/0.0075)=32.66 m³/s.||將單泵曲線換成共同總流量座標，與系統曲線交點比較實測揚程；逐台核對流量分配與逆止閥狀態，避免只看總出水量。~Convert individual pump curves to a common total-flow axis and compare the intersection with measured head. Check individual sharing and check-valve behavior instead of relying only on total discharge.||兩台老化程度不同會造成不均分流，甚至低流量機組接近不穩定區。忽略共用管損的加倍估算，通常會高估新增泵帶來的容量提升。~Unequal ageing creates unequal sharing and may place one unit near an unstable low-flow region. Doubling capacity while ignoring shared losses typically overstates the benefit of adding another pump.||並聯兩台泵的總流量不一定是單台的兩倍。~Two parallel pumps need not deliver twice the single-pump flow.
汽蝕餘裕與吸水~Cavitation margin and suction||吸水側壓力若接近水的汽化壓，氣泡形成與崩潰會傷害葉片。淨正吸入水頭需使用絕對壓力，且和廠商所定試驗條件分開比較。~Vapor bubbles form and collapse when suction pressure approaches vapor pressure, damaging impellers. Available net positive suction head uses absolute pressure and must be compared with the manufacturer test definition.||假設大氣水頭10.3 m、吸水靜高1.5 m、吸管損失0.8 m、汽化水頭0.3 m，NPSHa=10.3+1.5−0.8−0.3=10.7 m。~Assume atmospheric head 10.3 m, positive suction static head 1.5 m, suction loss 0.8 m and vapor head 0.3 m. NPSHa=10.3+1.5−0.8−0.3=10.7 m.||記錄水溫、水位與吸口壓力，核對入口旋渦和攔污柵堵塞；將振動、噪音與效率變化一起判讀，避免把任一聲音直接認定為汽蝕。~Record temperature, water level and suction pressure, checking intake vortices and screen blockage. Interpret vibration, noise and efficiency together instead of identifying cavitation from sound alone.||低水位與堵塞會同時降低可用吸入水頭，吸入空氣也會產生類似汽蝕的噪音。以冷水汽化壓代表熱天水況，可能誇大實際餘裕。~Low level and blockage both reduce available suction head, while entrained air can imitate cavitation noise. Using cold-water vapor pressure for warm conditions may exaggerate the available margin.||沒有明顯噪音不等於吸水條件具有足夠餘裕。~Absence of obvious noise does not prove adequate suction margin.
鹽水入侵質量平衡~Salt intrusion mass balance||淡水庫的鹽度受微量海水入侵影響，鹽水密度較大會先沿底部擴散。平均混合模型只能估算總鹽量，不能代表取水口短時濃度。~Small seawater intrusions affect a freshwater reservoir, and denser water can spread along the bottom first. A mean-mixing model estimates total salt but not short-term intake concentration.||假設淡水體積1 million m³、混入1000 m³海水鹽度35 g/kg，同密度完全混合；平均鹽度35×1000/1001000=0.03497 g/kg。~Assume freshwater volume 1 million m³ and intrusion 1000 m³ at 35 g/kg, equal densities and complete mixing. Mean salinity is 35×1000/1001000=0.03497 g/kg.||沿庫底至取水口布設深度剖面，校正電導與溫度，再以水量平衡核對入侵總量；保留底層尖峰而非只輸出全庫平均。~Profile depth from the bed to the intake, calibrating conductivity and temperature. Check intrusion volume against water balance and preserve bottom-layer peaks rather than reporting only a reservoir average.||稀釋後平均值很低仍可能有高鹽舌接近取水口，風浪混合也可能突然把底水抬升。只在表層採樣，會誤認鹽水已完全排除。~A low diluted mean can coexist with a saline tongue near an intake. Wind mixing may suddenly lift bottom water, while surface-only sampling can falsely suggest intrusion has been removed.||平均鹽度很低不代表所有深度水質都相同。~Low mean salinity does not imply uniform water quality with depth.
水力停留與營養鹽~Residence time and nutrients||停留時間影響營養鹽累積和藻類生長，但流動短路會讓部分水很快排出、其他水長期滯留。平均V/Q只是比較尺度，不能單獨預測生態反應。~Residence time influences nutrients and algae, but short-circuiting releases some water quickly while other regions stagnate. Mean V/Q is a comparison scale, not a complete ecological prediction.||假設有效庫容12 million m³、平均換水量6 m³/s，V/Q=2 million s=23.15 days；穩定完全混合近似，不代表所有水齡。~Assume effective volume 12 million m³ and average exchange 6 m³/s. V/Q=2 million s=23.15 days, a steady complete-mixing approximation rather than every parcel age.||以示蹤或導電度事件比較不同灣區到達時間，連同溶氧、溫度和葉綠素建立時序；區分物理滯留與外部營養鹽負荷增加。~Compare tracer or conductivity-event arrival times across reservoir arms and build oxygen, temperature and chlorophyll histories. Distinguish physical retention from increased external nutrient loading.||用總庫容忽略實際隔離死水區會誤判交換效率，增加出流也不必然沖走滯水。若未分離光照和水溫，不能把藻量變化全歸因於停留時間。~Ignoring isolated stagnant zones misjudges exchange, and more outflow need not flush them. Without separating light and temperature, changes in algae cannot be attributed entirely to hydraulic residence time.||縮短平均停留時間不保證每個灣區都被有效換水。~Shorter mean residence does not guarantee renewal in every reservoir arm.
攔污柵損失與堵塞~Screen losses and blockage||攔污柵保護設備卻增加水頭損失，堵塞使有效流通面積縮小。損失係數與速度必須使用相容的面積定義，否則會重複計算堵塞影響。~Screens protect equipment but consume head, and blockage reduces open area. Loss coefficient and velocity must use compatible area definitions to avoid counting the blockage effect twice.||取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設通過柵格的有效速度1.5 m/s、損失係數K=2，hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m；K已對應該速度定義，不再另加堵塞倍數。~Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume effective screen velocity 1.5 m/s and loss coefficient K=2. hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m; K corresponds to that velocity definition, without another blockage multiplier.||同步比較柵前後水位、流量與可見堵塞比例，建立清潔基線；檢查差壓管是否也被泥沙堵住，並將異常與雨後漂流物來源對照。~Compare upstream and downstream levels, flow and visible blockage against a clean baseline. Check pressure connections for sediment blockage and relate anomalies to storm-driven debris sources.||堵塞不均會把水流集中到少數開口，引發局部振動與吸氣。差壓增加也可能來自流量增大，因此未正規化的趨勢不能直接當作堵塞程度。~Uneven blockage concentrates flow through a few openings, promoting vibration and air entrainment. Increased differential head can also reflect increased flow, so an unnormalized trend does not directly measure blockage.||差壓上升不一定表示攔污柵堵塞程度相同增加。~Higher differential head does not uniquely measure increased screen blockage.
複合事件與失效組合~Compound events and failure combinations||暴雨、高海潮與電力限制可能同時發生，聯合機率取決於相關性。把各事件單獨罕見當成組合必定極罕見，會忽略共同氣象原因。~Heavy rain, high tide and power constraints can coincide, with joint probability depending on dependence. Individually rare events do not necessarily make their combination extremely rare when weather drives several conditions together.||假設一年高海潮事件機率0.1，且該條件下強降雨機率0.3，聯合機率0.03；若誤用無條件雨率0.1獨立相乘會得到0.01。~Assume annual high-tide event probability 0.1 and conditional heavy-rain probability 0.3. Joint probability is 0.03; incorrectly multiplying an unconditional rain probability 0.1 gives 0.01.||明確定義事件窗口、雨量門檻與潮位基準，核對歷史事件是否同時而非僅同年；用情境矩陣連結庫容、泵可用度與供電狀態。~Define event window, rainfall threshold and tidal datum, checking coincidence rather than merely the same calendar year. Link storage, pump availability and power condition in a scenario matrix.||樣本很少時條件機率不穩定，氣候變化又會改變共同分布。只列一個年機率而不說事件窗口，容易把短時設備容量與長期風險混為一談。~Conditional probabilities are unstable with sparse samples, and climate changes alter joint distributions. Reporting one annual probability without its event window confuses short-term capacity with long-term risk.||罕見暴雨與罕見海潮不能未經檢查就視為獨立。~Rare rainfall and rare tides cannot be assumed independent without evidence.
''')
 for i,ex,out,un in [(1,'.278*.75*60*2',25.02,'m3/s'),(2,'80*1800/3e6',.048,'m'),(3,'.65*20*math.sqrt(2*9.81*.5)',40.71719538,'m3/s'),(4,'1000*9.81*20*3/.8/1000',735.75,'kW'),(5,'math.sqrt(8/.0075)',32.65986,'m3/s'),(6,'10.3+1.5-.8-.3',10.7,'m'),(7,'35*1000/1001000',.03496503,'g/kg'),(8,'12e6/6/86400',23.148148,'days'),(9,'2*1.5**2/(2*9.81)',.2293578,'m'),(10,'.1*.3',.03,'probability')]:a('b225',i,ex,out,un)
